Linear algebra is the study of linear transformations on vectors, which represent points in a finite dimensional space.  The matrix-vector product y = A x is a linear combination of the columns of A.  The familiar definition,y_i = \sum_j A_{i,j} x_j

can also be viewed asy = \Bigg[ A_{:,1} \Bigg| A_{:,2} \Bigg| \dotsm \Bigg] \begin{bmatrix} x_1 \\ x_2 \\ \vdots \end{bmatrix}
= \Bigg[ A_{:,1} \Bigg] x_1 + \Bigg[ A_{:,2} \Bigg] x_2 + \dotsb .

